DESCRIPTION:National Sardines Day falls on November 24\, and no one appears
  to claim it: no fishery agency\, processor or trade body designates the d
 ate\, and nothing explains the choice of day. The fish is better documente
 d than the holiday. A sardine is not one species but a label shared by mor
 e than twenty\, and both American sardine industries — Maine's canneries
  and the Pacific fishery — are now gone or closed.\n\nhttps://todayceleb
 rates.com/holiday/national-sardines-day/
